WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.959 --> 00:00:03.444
- [Narrator] This pretty
lady's name is Asterix.

00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:05.567
And this is her son, Nate.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:08.900
They are northern white-cheeked gibbons.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.182
Their species is critically endangered.

00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:16.707
Only about 1,000 of them
are left in the world.

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:19.724
These gibbons are found
in Vietnam and Laos.

00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:22.336
They were also once
found in southern China,

00:00:22.336 --> 00:00:24.050
but are thought to be extinct there

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.300
due to logging of the gibbons' habitat.

00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:30.326
Asterix and Nate mainly eat fruit.

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:33.874
But Asterix has a sweet
tooth for dandelions.

00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:37.339
Infants are pale at birth
and turn black as they age.

00:00:37.339 --> 00:00:39.456
Female gibbons will change color again

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:41.252
as they near sexual maturity.

00:00:41.252 --> 00:00:43.528
Becoming golden or a deep red.

00:00:43.528 --> 00:00:45.111
Males remain black.

00:00:46.384 --> 00:00:47.897
Gibbons are known as small apes

00:00:47.897 --> 00:00:50.423
because of their slight stature.

00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:52.097
These primates have long arms,

00:00:52.097 --> 00:00:54.303
which are much longer than their legs.

00:00:54.303 --> 00:00:57.444
And they are muscular with
strong thighs and shoulders

00:00:57.444 --> 00:00:59.562
to help them swing through trees.

00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:01.601
The speed and agility of this species

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.517
has earned them the reputation

00:01:03.517 --> 00:01:06.867
as the trapeze artists
of the animal kingdom.

00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:10.367
This is the northern white-cheeked gibbon.

